Package: dimsprepr
Title: End-to-End Preprocessing of Direct-Injection Metabolomics Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("John Lennon", "Calorio", , "jllcalorio@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A complete, reproducible preprocessing pipeline for
    direct-injection mass spectrometry (DIMS) metabolomics data: missing
    value filtering, imputation, quality control (QC) based signal drift and
    batch correction (Kirwan et al. (2013) <doi:10.1007/s00216-013-6856-7>),
    normalization including probabilistic quotient normalization (Dieterle
    et al. (2006) <doi:10.1021/ac051632c>), transformation, scaling (van den
    Berg et al. (2006) <doi:10.1186/1471-2164-7-142>), and QC-based quality
    filtering (Broadhurst et al. (2018) <doi:10.1007/s11306-018-1367-3>).
    Supports multi-method mode: normalization, transformation, and scaling
    methods may each be supplied as character vectors, and the pipeline
    computes every combination while running the shared preprocessing steps
    only once.
